    id: "8ab56ca8e7109279a1b0",
    cat: "conflitti",
    title: "How Ukraine is taking the war 'deeper' into Russia",
    summary: "Ukrainian strikes have targeted key economic and military supply chains in recent weeks.",
    preview: "How Ukraine is taking the war 'deeper' into Russia Ukraine has struck two oil refineries in Russia, marking the latest attack where the targets have been deep inside Russia. President Volodymyr Zelensky said it was to limit oil revenues Moscow \"uses to finance\" its war. Attacks between Russia and Ukraine have intensified in recent weeks and mediation talks have not been fruitful. The BBC's Dan Johnson explains what Ukraine has been doing to effect ordinary business in Russia.",
    body: "How Ukraine is taking the war 'deeper' into Russia\n\nUkraine has struck two oil refineries in Russia, marking the latest attack where the targets have been deep inside Russia.\n\nPresident Volodymyr Zelensky said it was to limit oil revenues Moscow \"uses to finance\" its war.\n\nAttacks between Russia and Ukraine have intensified in recent weeks and mediation talks have not been fruitful.\n\nThe BBC's Dan Johnson explains what Ukraine has been doing to effect ordinary business in Russia.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- UkraineUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- RussiaUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- EuropeUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- War in UkraineUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
